## Decorator Pattern (Java)

The **Decorator Pattern** is a **structural design pattern** used to **add new behavior to an object dynamically without modifying its class**.

It wraps the original object inside a **decorator object**.

---

## Basic Idea

```text id="usn3de"
Component
    ↓
Concrete Component
    ↓
Decorator
    ↓
Enhanced behavior
```

The decorator **adds extra functionality** before or after the original method.

---

## Example Scenario

Coffee shop system:

```text id="3qxjuu"
Base Coffee
   ↓
Add Milk
   ↓
Add Sugar
```

Each addition **decorates the base coffee**.

---

## Step 1 — Component Interface

```java id="qzo3wq"
interface Coffee {

    String getDescription();
    int cost();

}
```

---

## Step 2 — Concrete Component

```java id="eexin5"
class BasicCoffee implements Coffee {

    public String getDescription(){
        return "Basic Coffee";
    }

    public int cost(){
        return 50;
    }

}
```

---

## Step 3 — Decorator Base Class

```java id="q2txag"
abstract class CoffeeDecorator implements Coffee {

    protected Coffee coffee;

    public CoffeeDecorator(Coffee coffee){
        this.coffee = coffee;
    }

}
```

---

## Step 4 — Concrete Decorators

Milk decorator:

```java id="8jth4v"
class MilkDecorator extends CoffeeDecorator {

    public MilkDecorator(Coffee coffee){
        super(coffee);
    }

    public String getDescription(){
        return coffee.getDescription() + " + Milk";
    }

    public int cost(){
        return coffee.cost() + 20;
    }

}
```

Sugar decorator:

```java id="qakwd4"
class SugarDecorator extends CoffeeDecorator {

    public SugarDecorator(Coffee coffee){
        super(coffee);
    }

    public String getDescription(){
        return coffee.getDescription() + " + Sugar";
    }

    public int cost(){
        return coffee.cost() + 10;
    }

}
```

---

## Step 5 — Client Code

```java id="u5hl8j"
public class Demo {

    public static void main(String[] args){

        Coffee coffee = new BasicCoffee();

        coffee = new MilkDecorator(coffee);
        coffee = new SugarDecorator(coffee);

        System.out.println(coffee.getDescription());
        System.out.println(coffee.cost());

    }

}
```

Output

```text id="bq2mle"
Basic Coffee + Milk + Sugar
80
```

---

## Advantages

```text id="5lkmld"
Adds functionality without modifying class
Follows Open-Closed Principle
Flexible behavior extension
```

---

