    .forEach(System.out::print);

// forEachOrdered → ordered output (slower)
list.parallelStream()
    .forEachOrdered(System.out::print);
```

---

## 4. Performance

```java id="feo5"
// forEach → faster (no ordering constraint)

// forEachOrdered → slower (maintains order)
```

---

## 5. Use Case

```java id="feo6"
// Use forEach → when order doesn't matter

// Use forEachOrdered → when order is important
```

---

## Summary 🔥

```java id="feo7"
// forEach        → unordered (parallel), faster
// forEachOrdered → ordered, slightly slower
```

---

## One-line Answer 💡

👉 `forEach()` may process elements in any order (especially in parallel), while `forEachOrdered()` **guarantees encounter order but may reduce performance**.

