## ForkJoinPool (Java 8)

👉 **Definition (crisp)**  
`ForkJoinPool` is a special thread pool used for **parallel task execution using divide-and-conquer (Fork/Join)**.

---

## Where Used?

```java id="fj1"
// used internally by parallel streams
list.parallelStream()
    .forEach(System.out::println);
```

👉 Uses:
```java id="fj2"
ForkJoinPool.commonPool()
```

---

## Core Idea 🔥

```java id="fj3"
// Fork → split task
// Join → combine result
```

---

## Example (Recursive Task)

```java id="fj4"
class SumTask extends RecursiveTask<Integer> {

    int[] arr;
    int start, end;

    SumTask(int[] arr, int start, int end) {
        this.arr = arr;
        this.start = start;
        this.end = end;
    }

    protected Integer compute() {

        if (end - start <= 2) {
            int sum = 0;
            for (int i = start; i < end; i++)
                sum += arr[i];
            return sum;
        }

        int mid = (start + end) / 2;

        SumTask left = new SumTask(arr, start, mid);
        SumTask right = new SumTask(arr, mid, end);

        left.fork();              // async
        int rightResult = right.compute(); // sync
        int leftResult = left.join();      // wait

        return leftResult + rightResult;
    }
}
```

---

## Execution

```java id="fj5"
ForkJoinPool pool = new ForkJoinPool();

int result = pool.invoke(new SumTask(arr, 0, arr.length));
```

---

## Internal Working 🔥

---

### 1. Task Splitting (Fork)

```java id="fj6"
// large task → split into smaller subtasks
```

---

### 2. Work-Stealing Algorithm 🚀

```java id="fj7"
// each thread has its own deque
// idle thread steals task from others
```

👉 Improves CPU utilization

---

### 3. Parallel Execution

```java id="fj8"
// tasks run on multiple threads
```

---

### 4. Join Phase

```java id="fj9"
// combine results of subtasks
```

---

## Key Components

```java id="fj10"
// RecursiveTask<T> → returns result
// RecursiveAction → no result
```

---

## Common Pool

```java id="fj11"
ForkJoinPool.commonPool();
```

👉 Shared by:
- Parallel streams  
- CompletableFuture  

---

## Key Points

- Divide & conquer  
- Work-stealing  
- High performance  
- Uses multiple CPU cores  

---

## One-line Answer 💡

👉 ForkJoinPool is a **parallel execution framework that splits tasks into smaller subtasks and uses work-stealing to efficiently utilize CPU cores**.

