Here are **industry-level ways** to find the **height of a binary tree** 👇

---

### 1. Recursive (Most Important 🔥 O(n))
```java id="ht1"
public class TreeHeight {

    static class Node {
        int val;
        Node left, right;
        Node(int v) { val = v; }
    }

    static int height(Node root) {
        if (root == null) return 0;

        return 1 + Math.max(
            height(root.left),
            height(root.right)
        );
    }
}
```

---

### 2. Iterative (Level Order BFS 🔥)
```java id="ht2"
import java.util.*;

static int height(Node root) {
    if (root == null) return 0;

    Queue<Node> q = new LinkedList<>();
    q.offer(root);
    int height = 0;

    while (!q.isEmpty()) {
        int size = q.size();

        for (int i = 0; i < size; i++) {
            Node curr = q.poll();

            if (curr.left != null) q.offer(curr.left);
            if (curr.right != null) q.offer(curr.right);
        }
        height++;
    }

    return height;
}
```

---

### 3. Using Stack (DFS Iterative 🔥)
```java id="ht3"
import java.util.*;

static int height(Node root) {
    if (root == null) return 0;

    Stack<Pair> stack = new Stack<>();
    stack.push(new Pair(root, 1));

    int max = 0;

    while (!stack.isEmpty()) {
        Pair p = stack.pop();
        Node node = p.node;
        int depth = p.depth;

        max = Math.max(max, depth);

        if (node.left != null)
            stack.push(new Pair(node.left, depth + 1));

        if (node.right != null)
            stack.push(new Pair(node.right, depth + 1));
    }

    return max;
}

static class Pair {
    Node node;
    int depth;
    Pair(Node n, int d) { node = n; depth = d; }
}
```

---

### 4. Height in Terms of Edges (Interview Variation 🔥)
```java id="ht4"
static int height(Node root) {
    if (root == null) return -1; // edge-based

    return 1 + Math.max(
        height(root.left),
        height(root.right)
    );
}
```

---

### 5. Generic Version 🔥
```java id="ht5"
class Node<T> {
    T val;
    Node<T> left, right;
}

static <T> int height(Node<T> root) {
    if (root == null) return 0;

    return 1 + Math.max(
        height(root.left),
        height(root.right)
    );
}
```

