Here are **industry-level implementations** of **Dijkstra’s Algorithm (Shortest Path)** 👇

---

### 1. Basic Dijkstra (Adjacency List + PriorityQueue 🔥🔥)
```java id="dj1"
import java.util.*;

public class Dijkstra {

    static class Pair {
        int node, dist;
        Pair(int n, int d) { node = n; dist = d; }
    }

    static int[] dijkstra(int V, List<List<Pair>> adj, int src) {
        int[] dist = new int[V];
        Arrays.fill(dist, Integer.MAX_VALUE);

        PriorityQueue<Pair> pq = new PriorityQueue<>((a, b) -> a.dist - b.dist);

        dist[src] = 0;
        pq.offer(new Pair(src, 0));

        while (!pq.isEmpty()) {
            Pair curr = pq.poll();
            int node = curr.node;
            int d = curr.dist;

            if (d > dist[node]) continue;

            for (Pair nei : adj.get(node)) {
                int newDist = d + nei.dist;

                if (newDist < dist[nei.node]) {
                    dist[nei.node] = newDist;
                    pq.offer(new Pair(nei.node, newDist));
                }
            }
        }

        return dist;
    }
}
```

