Here are **industry-level ways** to rotate an array by `k` positions 👇

---

### 1. Reverse Technique (Most Important 🔥)
```java id="rt1k9x"
import java.util.*;

public class RotateArray {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[] arr = {1,2,3,4,5,6,7};
        int k = 3;

        k = k % arr.length;

        reverse(arr, 0, arr.length - 1);
        reverse(arr, 0, k - 1);
        reverse(arr, k, arr.length - 1);

        System.out.println(Arrays.toString(arr));
    }

    static void reverse(int[] arr, int l, int r) {
        while (l < r) {
            int temp = arr[l];
            arr[l] = arr[r];
            arr[r] = temp;
            l++; r--;
        }
    }
}
```

