Here are **industry-level ways** to **rotate a linked list** 👇

---

### 1. Rotate Right by k (Most Important 🔥 O(n))
```java id="rot1"
public class RotateList {

    static class Node {
        int val;
        Node next;
        Node(int v) { val = v; }
    }

    static Node rotateRight(Node head, int k) {
        if (head == null || head.next == null || k == 0) return head;

        // find length & last node
        Node curr = head;
        int len = 1;

        while (curr.next != null) {
            curr = curr.next;
            len++;
        }

        // make circular
        curr.next = head;

        k = k % len;
        int steps = len - k;

        Node newTail = head;
        for (int i = 1; i < steps; i++) {
            newTail = newTail.next;
        }

        Node newHead = newTail.next;
        newTail.next = null;

        return newHead;
    }
}
```

