Here are **industry-level implementations** of a **Stack using two queues** 👇

---

### 1. Push Costly (Most Common 🔥)
```java id="sq1"
import java.util.*;

public class StackUsingQueues {
    Queue<Integer> q1 = new LinkedList<>();
    Queue<Integer> q2 = new LinkedList<>();

    void push(int x) {
        q2.offer(x);

        while (!q1.isEmpty()) {
            q2.offer(q1.poll());
        }

        // swap q1 and q2
        Queue<Integer> temp = q1;
        q1 = q2;
        q2 = temp;
    }

    int pop() {
        if (q1.isEmpty()) throw new RuntimeException("Empty");
        return q1.poll();
    }

    int top() {
        return q1.peek();
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        StackUsingQueues s = new StackUsingQueues();

        s.push(10);
        s.push(20);
        s.push(30);

        System.out.println(s.pop()); // 30
    }
}
```

