In Java, you can use a `switch` statement to handle different cases for enum values. Here's an example of how to use a `switch` statement with enum values:

```java
public enum DayOfWeek {
    SUNDAY, MONDAY, TUESDAY, WEDNESDAY, THURSDAY, FRIDAY, SATURDAY
}

public class EnumSwitchExample {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        DayOfWeek day = DayOfWeek.FRIDAY;

        switch (day) {
            case SUNDAY:
                System.out.println("It's a relaxing day!");
                break;
            case MONDAY:
                System.out.println("It's the start of the workweek.");
                break;
            case FRIDAY:
                System.out.println("It's almost the weekend!");
